This directory vendors `ascii_graphs`: a pure-Python, 1:1 port of the
`ascii-graphs` Scala library (https://github.com/mdr/ascii-graphs, MIT) — the
rendering engine that previously reached xrefer via `asciinet` + a JVM.

It is bundled here so xrefer renders ASCII graphs with no Java dependency.

  * Canonical source / tests: the ascii-graphs-py repository.
  * Internal imports are namespaced to `xrefer._vendor.ascii_graphs`.
  * Treat as read-only: do not refactor in place — re-sync from the canonical
    repo instead. Excluded from xrefer's ruff/coverage gates by design (the code
    deliberately mirrors the Scala structure to stay byte-exact).
  * License: MIT (see the canonical repo's LICENSE).
